>> title: Cream Gravy
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: milk, gravy, southern, roux, stovetop
>> counters: Meat and Three, Diner
>> aka: milk gravy, plain white gravy, pepper gravy, gravy for country fried steak
>> servings: 6
>> time: 25 min
>> pairs-with: country-fried-steak, meatloaf, cheese-grits
>> step.1: Season this one heavily and at the end. Sausage gravy is the same construction with browned sausage left in it, which is a different line on the board and cannot stand in for this on a steak.
>> step.2: whisk the flour into the fat 3 min
>> step.3: pour the milk in slowly, simmer 8 min
>> step.4: season, coarse pepper

Season this one heavily and at the end. Sausage gravy is the same construction with browned sausage left in it, which is a different line on the board and cannot stand in for this on a steak.

Whisk @frying fat{1/4%cup}(60 mL; poured back out of the steak pan), @all-purpose flour{1/4%cup}(32 g) in the #skillet{} for ~whisk{3%min}.

Pour @whole milk{3%cup}(710 mL) into @&(~1)pale roux{} a little at a time, then ~simmer{8%min}.

Season @&(~1)gravy{} with @black pepper{1 1/2%tsp}(coarsely ground), @kosher salt{1%tsp}.

Thin it with a splash more milk at the last moment. It sets up hard as it cools on the plate, so it should leave the pan looser than it will be eaten.
